{"id": "EUVD-2026-108734", "enisaUuid": "8ea847a8-7949-3b2c-b324-08ce001dac4d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: ctxfi: Fix memory leakage when clearing DAO input mappers\n\nCommit e576e7843c0d (\"ALSA: ctxfi: Simplify dao_clear_{left,right}_input() functions\")\ncentralized the DAO input mapper clearing logic in\ndao_clear_input(), but omitted the kfree() calls.\n\nIt removes the mapper entries from the list and sets their pointers\nto NULL without freeing the allocated array. This leaks memory each\ntime dao_clear_input() is called.\n\nStore the base pointer of the allocation before clearing the mapper\nentries and free the array after removing entries from the list.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:23:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:23:11", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f7dc71c1ce885f5d9f128037ebc75d9c0356e060", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0919d8dd19f92e12829055c75fced9a454d644bf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/593d46fc6af9a0178a46e77d6d24b20d2314165f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99068"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2fdaa786-9da8-321f-9d51-0ce07283d3fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "4b4e82d8-d257-3525-a0a2-a42aa186772f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e576e7843c0d65b82d4092e5b386d9fbf5bc10c3 <0919d8dd19f92e12829055c75fced9a454d644bf"}, {"id": "5fe31e4f-8002-3aad-b2d5-3fd114de0ace", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e576e7843c0d65b82d4092e5b386d9fbf5bc10c3 <593d46fc6af9a0178a46e77d6d24b20d2314165f"}, {"id": "6737de28-75b9-38f2-8c4a-a83336c5ef17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "77e2bec4-c260-3c81-9874-ad3612275faa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "8cda783b-ffad-3dcc-97df-0bb1ab888e48", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9144efc8-7b22-3882-8076-0c72ac6c897c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e576e7843c0d65b82d4092e5b386d9fbf5bc10c3 <f7dc71c1ce885f5d9f128037ebc75d9c0356e060"}, {"id": "a5ce205a-4455-3b9a-8e62-d937923bb2aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "290908c9-b502-35ae-a361-261ec0cd337c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}